[{"page":1,"str":"Date Published: 11/19/26","x":41.2,"y":54,"width":125.2,"height":12},{"page":1,"str":"ASSIST does not take the place of a counselor on your campus.","x":59.2,"y":128.2,"width":341.5,"height":12},{"page":1,"str":"It is intended to help students and counselors work together to establish","x":403.7,"y":128.2,"width":383.9,"height":12},{"page":1,"str":"an appropriate path toward transferring from a public California community college to a California university.","x":59.2,"y":145.5,"width":574.8,"height":12},{"page":1,"str":"IMPORTANT MAJOR DETAILS","x":35.2,"y":386.2,"width":290.9,"height":24},{"page":1,"str":"PROGRAMMING REQUIREMENT","x":35.2,"y":850.5,"width":317.6,"height":24},{"page":1,"str":"AP EXAM CREDIT","x":35.2,"y":997.5,"width":169.9,"height":24},{"page":1,"str":"The Computer Science and Engineering curriculum provides students with the education and training necessary to design, implement, test, and utilize the hardware and software of","x":47.2,"y":431.2,"width":728.8,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"digital computers and digital systems. The curriculum has components spanning from both the Computer Science and Electrical and Computer Engineering departments.","x":47.2,"y":444.7,"width":685.9,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"Admission to the Henry Samueli School of Engineering and Applied Science (HSSEAS) at UCLA is highly competitive. The most important selection criteria are completion of the","x":47.2,"y":472.5,"width":708.8,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"required preparatory courses and academic performance. Listed below are the lower division preparation courses for the major. All applicants must have a minimum transferable","x":47.2,"y":486,"width":716.2,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"cumulative GPA of 3.4. Preparatory courses should be completed by the end of the spring prior to Fall enrollment. HSSEAS admits students by major and does NOT consider applicants","x":47.2,"y":500.2,"width":737.1,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"for alternate majors.","x":47.2,"y":513.7,"width":82.7,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"To be considered for this major, you must complete the following courses by the end of spring before transfer:","x":47.2,"y":541.5,"width":442.6,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"All courses must be taken for a letter grade.","x":47.2,"y":611.2,"width":174.4,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"Applicants are not required to complete the HSSEAS General Education Requirements in order to be admitted, although it is beneficial for students to complete 1 course from each of","x":47.2,"y":638.2,"width":730.9,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"the following areas: arts, humanities, social sciences, and life sciences. Applicants can fulfill the lower division General Education requirement by completion of the Intersegmental","x":47.2,"y":652.5,"width":722,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"General Education Transfer Curriculum (IGETC) or California General Education Transfer Curriculum (Cal-GETC) .","x":47.2,"y":666,"width":450.8,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"Partial IGETC is NOT accepted.","x":47.2,"y":680.2,"width":122.1,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"For more information regarding this major and UCLA's transfer selection process, visit","x":47.2,"y":708,"width":345.2,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"https://admission.ucla.edu/","x":394.4,"y":708,"width":113.1,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":". If you still have specific questions, you may email the HSSEAS","x":507.5,"y":708,"width":252.7,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"admissions office at","x":47.2,"y":721.5,"width":80.4,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"ugradadm@seas.ucla.edu","x":129.6,"y":721.5,"width":105.6,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":".","x":235.2,"y":721.5,"width":2.4,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"PLEASE NOTE: The community college courses listed on this major agreement have been approved as substitutes to satisfy the admission preparation requirements for this major, but","x":47.2,"y":749.2,"width":735.6,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"they may not be exact equivalents of the UCLA courses listed. In addition, upper division requirements for the major may be satisfied by lower division community college course(s)","x":47.2,"y":763.5,"width":724.1,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"listed below, however, credit will be determined by the department after transfer.","x":47.2,"y":777,"width":327.9,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"One and a half years of Calculus through Multivariable,","x":76.5,"y":555.7,"width":221,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"•","x":70.6,"y":555.7,"width":3,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"One course in Linear Algebra,","x":76.5,"y":569.2,"width":118,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"•","x":70.6,"y":569.2,"width":3,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"One and a half years of Calculus Based Physics series [for Engineering majors] with Lab, and","x":76.5,"y":583.5,"width":370.6,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"•","x":70.6,"y":583.5,"width":3,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"One course in C++ (strongly preferred), C or JAVA.","x":76.5,"y":597,"width":198.4,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"•","x":70.6,"y":597,"width":3,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"C++ is the PREFERRED LANGUAGE for this major, however (Java, & C) are also acceptable programming courses.","x":47.2,"y":895.5,"width":449.1,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"NOTE: A course equivalent to UCLA's CS 31 is acceptable to meet the programming requirement for this major.","x":47.2,"y":923.2,"width":443.1,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"Credit awarded by UCLA as a result of AP exams for students in the School of Engineering may be found here:","x":47.2,"y":1042.5,"width":439,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"https://admission.ucla.edu/admitted-students/ap-credit-engineering","x":488.2,"y":1042.5,"width":280.1,"height":9.7},{"page":1,"str":"Major","x":35.2,"y":204,"width":35.2,"height":14.4},{"page":1,"str":"Articulation Agreement","x":73.4,"y":204,"width":139.4,"height":14.4},{"page":1,"str":"Computer Science and Engineering/B.S.","x":35.2,"y":237,"width":470.8,"height":28.3},{"page":